<attribute name="usageGuidance" nodeId="2aa64ddc"></attribute>
<attribute name="refinedDescription" nodeId="6eac44c3">&lt;p&gt;
    Build on the high level assumptions in the training strategy to further define the technical environment for training
    delivery, and the technical data requirements. This needs to be communicated to the technical team who will be
    responsible for preparing and delivering these for the training.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Training environment considerations include whether a live training environment will be used, or a sandbox, or a shared
    test environment with UAT. The data requirements should specify what kind of data is required, the period of time
    covered by the data, when fresh sets of data will be required if appropriate etc
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Conduct a session with IT to understand the systems and environments landscape and how they anticipate these will
        operate in relation to training.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Work with IT to ensure they document likely training data, technology and environment requirements.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Share requirements with the training manager and appropriate project teams who will be responsible for preparing
        and delivering on these requirements for the training.&lt;br /&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
</Element>
</reference>
